1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:15,635
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June twenty-second. The King and Queen of Belgium are visiting Japan, and the Emperor and Empress held a special dinner for them. Let's listen.

2
00:00:16,236 --> 00:00:18,995
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:19,696 --> 00:00:25,120
[News] ベルギーの国王と王妃が、日本に来ています。

4
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:31,460
[News] 天皇陛下と皇后陛下が、二人を迎えました。

5
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:38,304
[News] 夜には、皇居で特別な晩餐会が開かれました。

6
00:00:39,003 --> 00:00:47,164
[News] 晩餐会には、国王の家族や、たくさんの大切な客が集まりました。

7
00:00:47,863 --> 00:00:57,103
[News] 天皇陛下は、「両国の友好が、これからも続くことを願っています」と話しました。

8
00:00:57,804 --> 00:01:05,099
[News] 日本とベルギーは、長い間、仲の良い関係を続けてきました。

9
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:12,927
[News] 二つの国は、これまで150年以上、付き合ってきました。

10
00:01:13,628 --> 00:01:20,731
[News] 国王たちは、これから日本のいろいろな場所を訪れる予定です。

11
00:01:21,432 --> 00:01:28,272
[News] 二つの国の友好が、もっと深くなることが期待されています。

12
00:01:28,971 --> 00:01:30,603
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:31,203 --> 00:01:37,420
[Slow] ベルギーの国王と王妃が、日本に来ています。

14
00:01:38,219 --> 00:01:41,628
[Host] The King and Queen of Belgium are visiting Japan.

15
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:44,531
[Vocab] 国王

16
00:01:44,932 --> 00:01:51,891
[Host] It means a king. The two characters mean 'country' and 'king.' A king's wife is called a queen.

17
00:01:52,492 --> 00:01:58,924
[Slow] 天皇陛下と皇后陛下が、二人を迎えました。

18
00:01:59,724 --> 00:02:02,987
[Host] The Emperor and Empress welcomed the two of them.

19
00:02:03,587 --> 00:02:05,987
[Vocab] 迎える

20
00:02:06,388 --> 00:02:13,108
[Host] It means to welcome or greet someone — and also to go out and meet them, the way you'd go to pick someone up.

21
00:02:13,707 --> 00:02:20,716
[Slow] 夜には、皇居で特別な晩餐会が開かれました。

22
00:02:21,515 --> 00:02:27,084
[Host] In the evening, a special dinner banquet was held at the Imperial Palace.

23
00:02:27,683 --> 00:02:30,132
[Vocab] 特別

24
00:02:30,532 --> 00:02:37,204
[Host] It means special — a special day, a special guest. Its opposite is the word for ordinary.

25
00:02:37,804 --> 00:02:47,139
[Slow] 晩餐会には、国王の家族や、たくさんの大切な客が集まりました。

26
00:02:47,939 --> 00:02:52,836
[Host] At the banquet, the king's family and many important guests gathered.

27
00:02:53,436 --> 00:02:55,740
[Vocab] 集まる

28
00:02:56,139 --> 00:03:02,788
[Host] It means to gather or come together on its own. There's a partner verb for actively bringing things together.

29
00:03:03,388 --> 00:03:13,948
[Slow] 天皇陛下は、「両国の友好が、これからも続くことを願っています」と話しました。

30
00:03:14,747 --> 00:03:20,580
[Host] The Emperor said, 'I hope the friendship between our two countries continues from here on.'

31
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:23,556
[Vocab] 友好

32
00:03:23,955 --> 00:03:28,804
[Host] It means friendship, especially the friendly ties between countries.

33
00:03:29,403 --> 00:03:37,731
[Slow] 日本とベルギーは、長い間、仲の良い関係を続けてきました。

34
00:03:38,532 --> 00:03:43,116
[Host] Japan and Belgium have kept up friendly relations for a long time.

35
00:03:43,716 --> 00:03:46,020
[Vocab] 関係

36
00:03:46,419 --> 00:03:52,563
[Host] It means a relationship, or connection — between two people, or between two countries.

37
00:03:53,163 --> 00:04:01,300
[Slow] 二つの国は、これまで150年以上、付き合ってきました。

38
00:04:02,099 --> 00:04:07,620
[Host] The two countries have associated with each other for over a hundred and fifty years so far.

39
00:04:08,219 --> 00:04:10,524
[Vocab] 付き合う

40
00:04:10,924 --> 00:04:16,947
[Host] It means to keep company with, to associate with. It's also the everyday word for dating someone.

41
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:25,660
[Slow] 国王たちは、これから日本のいろいろな場所を訪れる予定です。

42
00:04:26,459 --> 00:04:30,444
[Host] The royals plan to visit various places in Japan from here.

43
00:04:31,043 --> 00:04:33,228
[Vocab] 予定

44
00:04:33,627 --> 00:04:39,387
[Host] It means a plan, or schedule — to have plans, or to be scheduled to do something.

45
00:04:39,987 --> 00:04:42,987
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

46
00:04:43,588 --> 00:04:46,348
[News] 今日のニュースです。

47
00:04:47,048 --> 00:04:52,471
[News] ベルギーの国王と王妃が、日本に来ています。

48
00:04:53,172 --> 00:04:58,812
[News] 天皇陛下と皇后陛下が、二人を迎えました。

49
00:04:59,512 --> 00:05:05,656
[News] 夜には、皇居で特別な晩餐会が開かれました。

50
00:05:06,355 --> 00:05:14,516
[News] 晩餐会には、国王の家族や、たくさんの大切な客が集まりました。

51
00:05:15,216 --> 00:05:24,456
[News] 天皇陛下は、「両国の友好が、これからも続くことを願っています」と話しました。

52
00:05:25,156 --> 00:05:32,451
[News] 日本とベルギーは、長い間、仲の良い関係を続けてきました。

53
00:05:33,151 --> 00:05:40,279
[News] 二つの国は、これまで150年以上、付き合ってきました。

54
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:48,084
[News] 国王たちは、これから日本のいろいろな場所を訪れる予定です。

55
00:05:48,783 --> 00:05:55,624
[News] 二つの国の友好が、もっと深くなることが期待されています。

56
00:05:56,324 --> 00:05:59,060
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

57
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:04,004
[Slow] だれが、日本に来ていますか。

58
00:06:04,803 --> 00:06:08,788
[Host] Who is visiting Japan? The King and Queen of Belgium.

59
00:06:09,387 --> 00:06:14,908
[Slow] 夜に、皇居で何が開かれましたか。

60
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:20,795
[Host] What was held at the Imperial Palace in the evening? A special dinner banquet.

61
00:06:21,396 --> 00:06:27,899
[Slow] 日本とベルギーは、何年ぐらい付き合ってきましたか。

62
00:06:28,699 --> 00:06:34,987
[Host] About how long have Japan and Belgium associated with each other? More than a hundred and fifty years.

63
00:06:35,588 --> 00:06:47,971
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

64
